{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-operator","title":"prop:hodge-star-operator","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":4244,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hodge-star-operator","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-graded]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-degree-zero]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-involution]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-classical-involution]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:fiber-metric-forms]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hodge-star-operator","line":7175,"source":"\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:hodge-star-operator}\\dcref{ch2:2-18}\n\n\n\\uses{prop:hodge-star-pointwise,prop:hodge-star-graded,prop:hodge-star-degree-zero,prop:hodge-star-involution,prop:hodge-star-classical-involution,prop:fiber-metric-forms}\nFor an oriented Riemannian $n$-manifold, there is a unique smooth Hodge star\n$*:\\Lambda^kT^*M\\to\\Lambda^{n-k}T^*M$ satisfying\n\\[\n\\omega\\wedge {*}\\eta=\\langle\\omega,\\eta\\rangle_gdV_g.\n\\]\nIt satisfies $*f=fdV_g$ for $k=0$ and\n$*^2\\omega=(-1)^{k(n-k)}\\omega$.\n\\end{proposition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f6467652d737461722d6f70657261746f72\"></span><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display